  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "The greatest common divisor of two integer numbers is 6. Which of the following cannot be the sum of the two integer numbers?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "318"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "272"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "186"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "462"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "906"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Both are multiples of 6",
    "body": "Both numbers are multiples of 6, so their sum is a multiple of 6. $272 = 6 \\cdot 45 + 2$ is not, so it is impossible.\n\nThe others are possible: e.g. $6$ and $312$ (gcd 6, sum 318), $6 + 180 = 186$, $6 + 456 = 462$, $6 + 900 = 906$ (in each case the second number is $6k$, and $\\gcd(6, 6k) = 6$).\n\n**Answer: (B) 272**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Divisibility tests",
    "body": "A multiple of 6 is even with digit sum divisible by 3. $318$: $3+1+8 = 12$ ✓; $272$: $2+7+2 = 11$ ✗; $186$: $15$ ✓; $462$: $12$ ✓; $906$: $15$ ✓. Only 272 fails.\n\n**Answer: (B) 272**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "number-theory"
  ],
  "difficulty": 1,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": null
 },
