  },
  "grade": "11-12",
  "points": 4,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "I look at our old church clock at 9 o'clock. How many full minutes must go past until the minute hand has just overtaken the hour hand?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "46"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "47"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "48"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "49"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "50"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Relative speed",
    "body": "The minute hand turns $6^\\circ$ per minute, the hour hand $0.5^\\circ$ per minute, so the minute hand gains $5.5^\\circ$ per minute. At 9:00 the hour hand is $270^\\circ$ ahead (measured clockwise from 12). The minute hand catches up after\n$$\\frac{270}{5.5} = \\frac{540}{11} = 49\\tfrac{1}{11} \\text{ minutes},$$\ni.e. at about 9:49:05. So 49 full minutes go past, and the minute hand overtakes the hour hand during the 50th minute.\n\n**Answer: (D) 49**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Check at 9:49",
    "body": "At 9:49 the minute hand is at $49 \\cdot 6^\\circ = 294^\\circ$ and the hour hand at $270^\\circ + 49 \\cdot 0.5^\\circ = 294.5^\\circ$: the minute hand is just $0.5^\\circ$ behind. About $\\frac{0.5}{5.5} = \\frac1{11}$ minute later (5.5 seconds) it overtakes. So the overtaking happens after 49 full minutes.\n\n**Answer: (D) 49**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "time-calendar",
   "rates"
  ],
  "difficulty": 2,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": "The hands meet 49 1/11 minutes after 9:00. The official key (D) 49 counts the full minutes that have passed when the minute hand overtakes the hour hand; reading the question as 'after how many full minutes has it already overtaken' would give 50."
 },
