  "prompt": "The lengths of three different sides of a rectangular prism are the three different roots of the equation $x^3 - 9x^2 + 26x - 24 = 0$. What is the total surface area of the solid?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "36"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "48"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "26"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "52"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "24"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Vieta",
    "body": "If the edge lengths are $a, b, c$, the surface area is $2(ab + bc + ca)$. By Vieta's formulas, $ab + bc + ca$ is the coefficient of $x$: $26$. So the surface area is $52$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 52**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Find the roots",
    "body": "$x = 2$ is a root: $8 - 36 + 52 - 24 = 0$. Dividing, $x^3 - 9x^2 + 26x - 24 = (x - 2)(x^2 - 7x + 12) = (x-2)(x-3)(x-4)$. A $2 \\times 3 \\times 4$ box has surface area $2(6 + 12 + 8) = 52$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 52**"
   }
  ],
