 {
  "id": "kangaroo-ca-2017-g1112-23",
  "bank": "kangaroo",
  "source": {
   "contest": "Canadian Math Kangaroo",
   "paper": "Grade 11-12",
   "year": 2017,
   "url": "https://api.mathkangaroo.ca/api/v1/media/2017/2017gr1112e.pdf",
   "number": 23
  },
  "grade": "11-12",
  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Consider the sequence $a_n$ with $a_1 = 2017$ and $a_{n+1} = \\frac{a_n - 1}{a_n}$. What is the value of $a_{2017}$?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$-2017$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2016}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\frac{2016}{2017}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "1"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "2017"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "E",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Period 3",
    "body": "- $a_2 = \\frac{2016}{2017}$\n- $a_3 = \\frac{\\frac{2016}{2017} - 1}{\\frac{2016}{2017}} = -\\frac{1}{2016}$\n- $a_4 = \\frac{-\\frac{1}{2016} - 1}{-\\frac{1}{2016}} = 2017 = a_1$\n\nSo the sequence repeats with period 3: $a_n = 2017$ whenever $n \\equiv 1 \\pmod 3$. Since $2017 = 3 \\cdot 672 + 1$, $a_{2017} = a_1 = 2017$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 2017** (the official key lists (B) $-\\frac{1}{2016}$, which would be the value of $a_{999}$)"
   },
   {
    "title": "Composition of the map",
    "body": "For $f(x) = 1 - \\frac1x$ we get $f(f(x)) = -\\frac{1}{x - 1}$ and $f(f(f(x))) = x$. Applying $f$ $2016 = 3 \\cdot 672$ times to $a_1$ returns $a_1$, so $a_{2017} = 2017$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 2017**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "sequences-series",
   "algebra"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": "Official Canadian key gives (B) -1/2016, which is the answer to the international version (a_999). For a_2017 as printed the sequence has period 3 and 2017 = 3*672 + 1, so a_2017 = a_1 = 2017 (E). Answer set to (E)."
 },
 {
  "id": "kangaroo-ca-2017-g1112-24",
  "bank": "kangaroo",
  "source": {
   "contest": "Canadian Math Kangaroo",
