  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "If $f(xy) = f(x + y)$ and $f(11) = 22$, what is the value of $f(33)$?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "11"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "22"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "33"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "44"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "66"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Put y = 0",
    "body": "With $y = 0$: $f(x \\cdot 0) = f(x + 0)$, i.e. $f(0) = f(x)$ for every $x$. So $f$ is constant, and $f(33) = f(11) = 22$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 22**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Without using 0",
    "body": "With $y = 1$: $f(x) = f(x + 1)$ for all $x$, so $f$ takes the same value at all numbers that differ by an integer. In particular $f(33) = f(11 + 22) = f(11) = 22$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 22**"
   }
  ],
